invariant: INV-26
file: gcm_vaes.c
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: gcm_vaes.c drops the target attribute that turns VAES, VPCLMULQDQ
  and AVX2 on for its own functions, so the kernels compile only where the
  whole object is built with those flags, and an object built that way
  runs them in code the caller's CH_CPU_VAES bit never chose. The script
  compiles the file for x86-64 in a host object with no flag beyond the
  host object's define, and requires the three kernels on 256-bit VAESENC
  and VPCLMULQDQ.

--- old
#ifdef __clang__
#pragma clang attribute push(__attribute__((target("aes,pclmul,avx2,vaes,vpclmulqdq"))),           \
                             apply_to = function)
#else
#pragma GCC push_options
#pragma GCC target("aes,pclmul,avx2,vaes,vpclmulqdq")
#endif
--- new
#ifdef __clang__
#pragma clang attribute push(__attribute__((cold)), apply_to = function)
#else
#pragma GCC push_options
#endif
